PATCH 573: the mesh loader chain -- 19d1/1a45/183f/1692/1735 rebuilt, the FILEMGR leaves carry DS and CF,
extender ops 0x3c/0x4c, the resource relocation callback 15c2, and three arg-less cockpit blits.

board:0025.  With 571 (the model budget) and 572 (0c7f's unlink) the STRSEG:0x802 model walk reached
every model, and each load failed one level down.  The chain, read from the asm and rebuilt 1:1:

  183f  the per-model LOD driver (lod&8: 19d1 + 1a45('00') + 197b + 1a45('08') + 1996; lod&0x10:
        1a45('16') + 19b9; lod&0x20: 1a45('32')); every CF hard-wired false before -> now g_fist_cf
        from the loaders, the 18dc release tail with the failing lod class in cx.
  19d1  the .MAL loader: [0x550] name, ".MAL" swapped into [0x748]/[0x74a], 1 KB through [0xe4] into
        DGROUP:0x26e4[idx], [0x384] batch load into that segment (DAT_1000_2b5e for 2593), extender op
        0x4c (cx=dx=seg, si=0, di=0x300) -> the 256-byte palette-remap LUT at seg:0x300.  Ghidra had
        fabricated the CFs as `0xd91b < idx*2` and called every vector without arguments.
  1a45  the streaming mesh loader: [0x38c] open, 16-byte record headers through [0x394], the facing
        indices rotated by -0x20 mod 0x40, the descriptor slot word[rec+0x44+2*min], the scratch
        segment through [0xe4] (handle DGROUP:0x3ad6, freed and re-allocated per record by 184b's
        bit-7 path), the body read with DS = that segment, word[0x276c+idx] = the part count, the
        texel translation through the .MAL LUT unless byte[0x3ada], op 0x3c (cx = es:[0], dx:si =
        es:0) whose EDX goes to es:[2], the final allocation into the descriptor and the rep movsb,
        the close with the slot in bx.  The fabricated open-CF had leaked 276e's four slots (0025).
  1692  1684's twin (byte[0x3ada]=0xff, the two models without palette translation): 183f's CF and
        `call 1724` = `pop ax ; stc ; ret` (return CF=1 when the facing-0 descriptor is unallocated).
  1735  the third table vector (TREES, three entries) promoted and dispatched from 4308 like 1684; it
        had trapped, so TREES.* never loaded.
  1774  [0xe4]: bytes -> paragraphs with the 17-bit carry, then 177f (patch 571) -- the guard byte
        was DAT_2000_d1d4 (g_mem+0x2d1d4, the SS=0x2ba9 placeholder), a stray byte in the DOS heap.
  27f7/2871  the READ leaf's INT 21h reads the caller's DS:DX; DS is threaded (1a45 reads into the
        scratch segment); the leaf's CF is INT 21h's.  276e: CF=1 when all four slots are taken, CF=0
        on the no-variant exit; 2825 and 2593 return their CF (open failures) through g_fist_cf.
  11f4  (fist_ext.c) extender op 0x3c: the source is (dx<<4)+si+[0x807] in the guest-RAM window =
        g_mem (Ghidra read [0x807] as the DGROUP word), and the append position inside the model
        block -- the handler's EDX -- is published in g_fist_ext_edx_out.
  gate  (tools/native_main.c) ops 0x3c (11f4 with the patch-471 register lanes) and 0x4c (123f ->
        9e60: the .MAL palette remap).  fist_dos.c: INT 21h AH=43 is an existence probe, as DOS's --
        the FILEMGR's variant walks (276e/2733/26fc/2825) select the on-disk file with it.
  15c2  the resource-object relocation callback 1541 installs ([S+4]=0x15c2, [S+6]=CS) and the
        MEMMGR's 1019 far-calls with AX=old paragraph, DX=new, BX=kind: `call cs:[bx+0x15c9] ; retf`
        over {15d9, 15c8 x6, 15fa}.  Unpromoted before, so every block move left the sprite directory
        [0x4f0] pointing at the old paragraphs; 15d9 (move the entries' segment words by dx-ax) and
        15fa (re-home them to dx) rebuilt -- Ghidra had host-deref'd es:[0]/es:[2] and dropped [0x4f0].
        1019 passes bx as the third argument.
  7fcd/5a1d/3823  three arg-less MGA blit sites of patch 520/531's class, reached in the AZER1
        self-play once real sprite sheets were loaded: 7fcd (the azimuth needle, [0x6c8] x2) blitted a
        stack value as its sprite id -> a wild record whose header height ran 298a thousands of rows
        past the 288x81 view surface, over MSPRITE2's block and its directory header; 5a1d ([0x60a]
        al=0x17, [0x61a] al=1, [0x6c8] ax=0xfc8) and 3823 (ax=[bx+0x32], bx=0x6c16) likewise.  3823's
        rect right edge is left + the WIDTH byte (384f `mov dh,0` before 3860 `add ax,dx`); patch 391
        added the whole header word.  121 sites of the class remain (board:0015).

Measured (FIST_OPENLOG vs the oracle's LD_PRELOAD open trace, AZER1 accept): the 160 model files now
open in the original's order, file for file (M1_A.MAL .. HIND.M32, TREES included); MSN2.MS3,
MSPRITE5.BIN, MSPRITE1.BIN, M1CON.MRL follow as in the original.  Still different: the original opens
BURM_D2.KLC/BURM_C2.KLC five times between the models and MSN2.MS3 (the TCB's default map names at
DGROUP:0xea7c -- an extender op the gate does not run yet), RESOURCE.RES x4 where the port reads the
loose *.MEG files, WVSOUNDS.BIN/DSOUNDS.BIN (sound), INTRO.MS3 (boot); the port additionally opens
MSPRITE2.BIN/M2CON.MRL/CCV.MRL after the player's vehicle dies (7eb7's view reset).  The self-play
runs to DEFEAT (own side lost) at 3:38 mission time without a crash or hang; the original's DEFEAT
comes at 5:49 -- the sim is not yet congruent (board:0017).
